nes around White's B1 and C2, and the game tipped here."}, {"turn": 32, "text": "The 20k's A7 lost 23.6 points of its own, bringing the lead from -31.1 back to -7.5 (the engine preferred A6). For one move the game was close again, and Black had a real chance to recover."}, {"turn": 35, "text": "B6 was the worst move of the game, 26.9 points lost (-6.2 → -33.1). The engine's choice was A5. Black had just got back into a game that was within 7 points, and this threw it away."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Every script only played moves the player named through mcp__go__play, then parsed the returned board into groups and liberties (the stored 'inspect' function), counted final area, and wrote the log, SGF and review files with apply_patch. None of it loops over candidate moves, ranks moves, or plays a sequence forward.", "stop": false}}